====================================================================================================
LINES OF CODE: the shared routine and what each regime needs beyond it
====================================================================================================
  shared routine residual()                     30 lines   all five regimes call it unchanged
  (1) law: identity-table test                   2 lines   zero residual is "B is a function of A"; a law also needs the table to be the identity
  (1) law: term enumerator                      15 lines   the group-by runs on the TERM space (key = whole column), not on the row space
  (2) inverse: guard from a pool                 9 lines   plus the guard pool itself (enumerated Boolean terms) and the grid design (padding)
  (2) inverse: witness search                   18 lines   the routine returns the table (b,c)->a, i.e. the specification; the term is a search
  (3) residual: Y minus U                        6 lines   type-specific; undefined when list lengths differ
  (3) residual: to the position space            3 lines   a constant offset on lists of varying length is constant only per position
  (3) residual: integer code                     5 lines   L(R) is a code length on values, not an entropy of a group-by
  (3) residual: guard for the disagreeing rows   9 lines   plus the guard pool; then a separate problem for ?else
  (4) congruence                                 0 lines   nothing; choosing q is a separate search (verify-quotients: 19 s)
  (5) soft verb table                            0 lines   nothing; probe design (count, edge cases) is outside the routine
